957acd\"><img src=\"https://link.axios.com/img/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94asso4k.94l8/a1a528c2.gif\" alt=\"\" border=\"0\" /></a></td>\r\n<td style=\"padding-right:3.5%\" align=\"right\"> <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48366884.425852/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYXhpb3MuY29tL25ld3NsZXR0ZXJzL2F4aW9zLWZpbmlzaC1saW5lLTc0NTE2YTZmLWFhMzgtNDI0ZC05ODUwLTUxMjAwZGYzMDczOS5odG1sP3V0bV9zb3VyY2U9bmV3c2xldHRlciZ1dG1fbWVkaXVtPWVtYWlsJnV0bV9jYW1wYWlnbj1uZXdzbGV0dGVyX2F4aW9zZmluaXNobGluZSZzdHJlYW09dG9w/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB829c6bdc\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"b\" style=\"color:#222;font-size:13px;font-family:'gordita',Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;text-decoration:underline\">View in browser</a> </td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</table>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td height=\"30\" style=\"height:30px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>  <tr>\r\n<td style=\"text-align:center;line-height:1.3\"> </td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td height=\"16\" style=\"height:16px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td style=\"text-align:center;line-height:1\">\r\n<span class=\"s\" style=\"font-size:44px;font-family:'gorditamedium',Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#008dc8;letter-spacing:-1px;line-height:1\"> Axios Finish Line </span>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"text-align:center;line-height:1.5;padding-bottom:35px;padding-top:10px\">\r\n<span class=\"b\" style=\"font-size:13px;color:#222;font-family:'gorditamedium',Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">By  Mike Allen and Erica Pandey and Jim VandeHei  <span style=\"margin:0 6px\">&middot;</span> Nov 10, 2026 </span>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td class=\"v\" style=\"font-size:17px;font-family:Georgia,serif;line-height:1.75;color:#222;letter-spacing:-0.1px;padding:0 3.5%\"><p><strong>Welcome back! </strong><em>Smart Brevity™ count: 257 words … 1 min. Copy edited by Amy Stern.</em></p></td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0;border-bottom:10px solid #f5f5f5\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>      <tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:20px 3.5% 10px;line-height:1.5\">\r\n<span class=\"b k\" style=\"font-size:27px;font-family:'gorditamedium',Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#222;letter-spacing:-0.1px;line-height:1.5\">  1 big thing: Veterans who keep serving </span>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>   <tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td> <img src=\"https://images.axios.com/z0DLva10wdHXKOHKjr3VsCh-xv0=/1920x1080/smart/2022/05/25/154246-1653493366619.jpg\" width=\"600\" style=\"width:100%\" id=\"item02\" alt=\"Illustration of military camouflage with patterns in the shape of reaching hands\"> </td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0\">\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:0 3.5%;line-height:1.3\">\r\n<span class=\"b\" style=\"font-size:13px;color:#848484\"> <p>Illustration: Sarah Grillo/Axios</p> </span>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td height=\"15\" style=\"height:15px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr> <tr>\r\n<td class=\"v\" style=\"padding:0 3.5%;line-height:1.75;font-size:17px;font-family:Georgia,serif;color:#222;letter-spacing:-0.1px\"><p><strong>Veterans volunteer,</strong> help neighbors and give to charity more than the average American.</p><ul><li><strong>Why it matters: </strong>For many veterans, service is a way of life — and it continues long after they've hung up their uniforms.</li></ul><p><strong>💡 Data du jour: </strong>Veterans who volunteer spend an average of 93 hours a year serving, compared with 69 hours for other volunteers, <em>according to the <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48366884.425852/aHR0cHM6Ly9uY29jLm9yZy93cC1jb250ZW50L3VwbG9hZHMvMjAyNi8wMS8yMDI1LVZFVFMtQ0hJLTEuMjYuMjYucGRmP3V0bV9zb3VyY2U9bmV3c2xldHRlciZ1dG1fbWVkaXVtPWVtYWlsJnV0bV9jYW1wYWlnbj1uZXdzbGV0dGVyX2F4aW9zZmluaXNobGluZSZzdHJlYW09dG9w/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aBfbd31baa\" target=\"_blank\">2025 Veterans Civic Health Index</a>.</em></p><ul><li><strong>Americans who've served</strong> are also likelier to donate to charity (56% vs. 50% of nonveterans).</li><li><strong>Veterans are also</strong> slightly more likely to talk to their neighbors and help them with transportation, errands or child care.</li></ul><p><strong>Zoom in: </strong>On and around Veterans Day, many veterans turn that spirit of giving back toward their own communities.</p><ul><li>🍜 <strong>In San Diego,</strong> veterans, active-duty service members and other volunteers organized <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48366884.425852/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cubmJjc2FuZGllZ28uY29tL25ld3MvbG9jYWwvdS1zLXZldGVyYW5zLWhlbHBpbmctdmV0ZXJhbnMtc2FuLWRpZWdvLWZvb2QtZHJpdmUtc3VwcG9ydHMtbWlsaXRhcnktZmFtaWxpZXMvNDA5ODkwMi8_dXRtX3NvdXJjZT1uZXdzbGV0dGVyJnV0bV9tZWRpdW09ZW1haWwmdXRtX2NhbXBhaWduPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXJfYXhpb3NmaW5pc2hsaW5lJnN0cmVhbT10b3A/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aBea052024\" target=\"_blank\">a food drive</a> on Sunday for military families struggling to make ends meet.</li><li><strong>🦃 In southeastern Michigan, </strong>VETLIFE — a veteran-founded nonprofit — is working with Kroger to provide <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48366884.\" target=\"_blank\">free Thanksgiving dinners</a> to 400 veteran and active-duty military families.</li><li>🔨 <strong>In Sacramento,</strong> veterans are <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48366884.425852/aHR0cHM6Ly9oYWJpdGF0Z3JlYXRlcnNhYy5vcmcvZ2V0LWludm9sdmVkL3ZldGVyYW5zLXNlcnZpY2UtZGF5P3V0bV9zb3VyY2U9bmV3c2xldHRlciZ1dG1fbWVkaXVtPWVtYWlsJnV0bV9jYW1wYWlnbj1uZXdzbGV0dGVyX2F4aW9zZmluaXNobGluZSZzdHJlYW09dG9w/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aBb1c3ce90\" target=\"_blank\">teaming up tomorrow</a> to repair fellow veterans' homes through Habitat for Humanity's Veterans Service Day.</li></ul><p><strong>The bottom line: </strong>Tomorrow is a chance to honor and say thanks to some of the most generous members of our community.</p></td>\r\n</tr> <tr><td align=\"center\" style=\"padding:20px 3.5% 25px\">   <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48366884.425852/aHR0c